        "id": 209546,
        "name": "dprcooke",
        "username": "dprcooke",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dprcooke/{size}/1961_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-30T03:53:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>In fairness to C&amp;A, they did mention way back near the beginning that Biomancer was more Interlude than full episode material.</p>\n<p>But still, lots of unanswered questions here. And some new ones. Like, what has he actually been DOING for the past 1800 years?  As for his “plans”, is it just “cause minor annoyances to allieve my boredom while I simply wait to outlive my enemies”?</p>\n<p>My guess is that either there just isn’t much story for Boimancer, or there’s important story in the RPG starter kit, and C&amp;A were trying to avoid that.</p>\n<p>Then again, after listening to the episode like 4/5 times, I’m convinced of my original post’s theory that this episode was relatively light on info because C&amp;A have already been replaced by flesh children copies. That hilarious little bit at the end was just a ruse to fool us…</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:39:40.947Z",
